<rml>
<head><title>Octaryn</title><link type="text/rcss" href="game.rcss"/><link type="text/rcss" href="inventory.rcss"/></head>
<body>
<div id="hud">
  <div id="crosshair"><div class="cross-horizontal"/><div class="cross-vertical"/></div>
  <div class="hotbar-dock"><div class="held-name"><img id="selected-block" src="../Atlases/basegame-color.png" rect="0 0 32 32"/><span id="selected-name">Hand</span></div><div id="hotbar"/></div>
</div>
<div id="diagnostics" class="panel diagnostics"><div class="stats-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Performance</span><div><b id="fps">0</b><small> FPS</small></div></div><div id="metrics"/><div id="samples" class="muted tiny"/></div>
<div id="scrim" class="hidden"/>
<div id="loading-veil" class="hidden"/>
<div id="menu" class="modal hidden">
  <div class="brand">OCTARYN</div>
  <div class="panel menu-panel">
    <div class="panel-scroll">
    <div id="settings-screen">
      <div class="heading"><h1>World &amp; display</h1></div>
      <div class="settings-grid">
        <div class="settings-column"><h2>Display</h2>
          <button id="display" row="0" class="setting"><span>Monitor</span><b id="display-value"/></button>
          <button id="resolution" row="1" class="setting"><span>Resolution</span><b id="resolution-value"/></button>
          <button id="fullscreen" row="2" class="setting"><span>Window mode</span><b id="fullscreen-value"/></button>
          <button id="distance" row="3" class="setting" title="Loaded world radius in blocks; each column is 32 blocks wide. Also limits available ray-traced geometry. Larger worlds cost streaming time, memory and ray-scene work."><span>View distance</span><b id="distance-value"/></button>
          <button id="vsync" action="cycle-vsync" class="setting" title="Off presents immediately. On waits for the display. Mailbox keeps extra swap images when uncapped."><span>VSync</span><b id="vsync-value"/></button>
          <button id="frame-cap" action="cycle-frame-cap" class="setting" title="Limits how many frames the client presents each second. Separate from the anti-aliasing resolution target."><span>Frame cap</span><b id="frame-cap-value"/></button>
          <button action="open-fsr" class="setting"><span>Anti Aliasing</span><b>Configure</b></button>
          <button action="open-lighting" class="setting"><span>Light &amp; atmosphere</span><b>Configure</b></button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="materials"><h2>Materials</h2><button id="pom" row="10" class="setting toggle"><span>Parallax depth</span><b id="pom-value"/></button><button id="pbr" row="11" class="setting toggle"><span>Physical materials</span><b id="pbr-value"/></button></div>
      <div class="footer"><button row="12" id="apply" class="primary">Apply &amp; return</button><button row="13">Close</button><button row="14" class="quiet danger">Exit game</button></div>
    </div>
    <div id="fsr-screen" class="hidden">
      <div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">Anti Aliasing</div><h1>Image quality &amp; performance</h1></div>
      <button id="fsr-mode" action="fsr-mode" class="setting"><span>Quality preset</span><b id="fsr-mode-value"/></button>
      <p id="fsr-description" class="fsr-description"/>
      <div id="fsr-resolution" class="fsr-resolution"/>
      <div class="fsr-columns"><div>
        <h2>Clarity</h2>
        <button id="fsr-sharpen" action="fsr-sharpen" class="setting"><span>Sharpening</span><b id="fsr-sharpen-value"/></button>
        <div class="fsr-slider"><label for="fsr-sharpness">Sharpness</label><b id="fsr-sharpness-value"/><input id="fsr-sharpness" fsr-field="sharpness" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1"/></div>
        <div class="fsr-slider"><label for="fsr-scale">Custom render scale</label><b id="fsr-scale-value"/><input id="fsr-scale" fsr-field="scale" type="range" min="33.334" max="100" step="0.1"/></div>
        <p class="fsr-help">Higher sharpness emphasizes edges. Custom scale applies when the Custom preset is selected.</p>
      </div><div>
        <h2>Adaptive performance</h2>
        <button id="fsr-dynamic" action="fsr-dynamic" class="setting"><span>Dynamic resolution</span><b id="fsr-dynamic-value"/></button>
        <div class="fsr-slider"><label for="fsr-target">Target frame rate</label><b id="fsr-target-value"/><input id="fsr-target" fsr-field="target" type="range" min="30" max="240" step="1"/></div>
        <div class="fsr-slider"><label for="fsr-min">Minimum scale</label><b id="fsr-min-value"/><input id="fsr-min" fsr-field="min" type="range" min="33.334" max="100" step="0.1"/></div>
        <div class="fsr-slider"><label for="fsr-max">Maximum scale</label><b id="fsr-max-value"/><input id="fsr-max" fsr-field="max" type="range" min="33.334" max="100" step="0.1"/></div>
        <p class="fsr-help">Uses GPU load to adjust resolution. CPU limits can prevent reaching the target. Native AA always stays at 100%.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="footer"><button action="fsr-apply" class="primary">Apply &amp; return</button><button action="fsr-back">Back</button><button action="fsr-reset" class="quiet">Reset</button></div>
      <p class="fsr-help">Changes take effect when applied. Off is the default. Anti aliasing does not generate extra frames.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="main-screen" class="hidden">
      <div class="heading"><h1>Play</h1></div>
      <div class="menu-actions"><button row="2" class="primary">Singleplayer</button><button row="3">Multiplayer</button><button row="4">Settings</button><button row="14" class="quiet danger">Exit game</button></div>
    </div>
    <div id="pause-screen" class="hidden">
      <div class="heading"><h1>Paused</h1></div>
      <div class="pause-actions"><button row="2" class="primary pause-resume">Return to world</button>
        <button action="open-inventory">Inventory &amp; equipment</button><button action="open-creative">Creative blocks</button>
        <button row="4">World &amp; display</button><button action="open-lighting">Light &amp; atmosphere</button>
        <button row="5">Save to main menu</button><button action="open-controls">Controls</button>
        <button row="14" class="quiet danger pause-save-exit">Save and Exit</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="controls-screen" class="hidden">
      <div class="heading"><h1>Controls</h1></div>
      <div class="controls-columns">
        <div><h2>Explore</h2>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Move</span><b>W A S D</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Jump / fly up</span><b>Space</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Fly down</span><b>Q / Left Shift</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Sprint</span><b>Left Ctrl</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Toggle flight</span><b>F / F5</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Zoom</span><b>Z</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Game menu</span><b>Escape</b></div>
        </div>
        <div><h2>Build &amp; arrange</h2>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Inventory</span><b>I / E</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Creative blocks</span><b>B</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Hotbar slot</span><b>1 - 0 / Wheel</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Break / place</span><b>LMB / RMB</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Pick block</span><b>MMB</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Performance</span><b>F3</b></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span>Lighting</span><b>F6</b></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="controls-note">Drag items between slots, or click to hold a stack. Right-click takes or places one item. T drops one; Ctrl+T drops the whole stack. Creative blocks are unlimited.</p>
      <div class="footer"><button action="back-pause" class="primary">Back to game menu</button></div>
    </div>
    <div id="worlds-screen" class="hidden"><div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">Singleplayer</div><h1>Your worlds</h1></div><p class="menu-hint">Select a world or create a new one.</p><div class="world-list">
      <button id="world-0" row="2"><b>World 1</b><small id="world-0-state"/></button><button id="world-1" row="3"><b>World 2</b><small id="world-1-state"/></button><button id="world-2" row="4"><b>World 3</b><small id="world-2-state"/></button>
      </div><label>New world name</label><input id="world-name" type="text" maxlength="15"/>
      <div class="footer"><button row="6" class="primary">Play selected</button><button row="7">Create world</button><button row="10">Save</button></div><div class="footer"><button row="8" class="danger">Delete selected</button><button id="delete-confirm" row="9" class="danger hidden">Confirm delete</button><button row="13">Back</button></div>
    </div>
    <div id="servers-screen" class="hidden"><div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">Multiplayer</div><h1>Join a server</h1></div><p class="menu-hint">Enter a server address and port.</p><label>Server address</label><input id="server-address" type="text" maxlength="15"/><label>Port</label><input id="server-port" type="text" maxlength="5"/><p class="menu-hint">Example: 127.0.0.1:17531</p><div class="footer"><button row="4" class="primary">Connect</button><button row="5">Local server</button><button row="13">Back</button></div></div>
    <div id="loading-screen" class="hidden"><div class="heading"><h1 id="loading-title">Preparing world</h1></div><div class="loading-panel"><div class="loading-bar"><div id="loading-bar-fill"/></div><p id="loading-status" class="loading-status">Starting...</p><p id="loading-detail" class="loading-detail"/></div></div>
    <div id="menu-status" class="status"/>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div id="inventory" class="modal hidden">
  <div class="panel inventory-panel">
    <div class="inventory-heading"><div><h1>Inventory</h1></div><button action="close-inventory" class="quiet close-inventory">Close</button></div>
    <div class="inventory-tabs"><button id="inventory-tab" action="tab-inventory" class="selected">Inventory &amp; equipment</button><button id="creative-tab" action="tab-creative">Creative blocks</button><span class="creative-badge">Creative</span></div>
    <div id="inventory-page">
      <div class="inventory-columns">
        <div class="inventory-storage"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Backpack</h2><small>50 slots / first row is your hotbar</small></div>
          <div id="inventory-slots" class="slot-grid"/>
          <div class="inventory-tools"><button action="sort-inventory" class="quiet">Sort backpack</button><button action="clear-slot" class="quiet">Clear selected slot</button></div>
          <p class="inventory-note">Drag to move. Right-click for one. T to drop. Creative blocks are unlimited.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="equipment-panel"><h2>Equipment</h2>
          <div class="equipment-row hand-equipment"><div class="equipment-symbol">+</div><div><span>Tool</span><b id="equipment-hand-name">Hand</b><small id="equipment-hand-state">Ready to build</small></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="creative-page" class="hidden">
      <div class="creative-target"><span>Add blocks to hotbar slot</span><div id="creative-hotbar" class="target-hotbar"/></div>
      <div class="creative-toolbar"><label for="creative-search">Find a block</label><input id="creative-search" type="text" maxlength="64"/><span id="creative-count"/></div>
      <div class="creative-categories"><button action="category" category="all" class="selected">All blocks</button><button action="category" category="terrain">Terrain</button><button action="category" category="nature">Nature</button><button action="category" category="lighting">Lighting</button><button action="category" category="fluids">Fluids</button></div>
      <div class="creative-results"><div id="creative-blocks" class="slot-grid"/><div id="creative-empty" class="empty-results hidden"><h2>No blocks found</h2><p>Try another name or choose All blocks.</p></div></div>
      <p class="inventory-note">Select a hotbar slot above, then choose a block to fill it. Blocks are unlimited in Creative.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="inventory-footer"><span id="inventory-status">Ready to build.</span><button action="close-inventory" class="primary">Return to world</button></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div id="cursor-item" class="hidden"><span id="cursor-icon"/><span id="cursor-count"/></div>
<div id="inventory-tooltip" class="hidden"/>
<div id="inventory-toast" class="hidden"/>
<div id="lighting" class="modal hidden"><div class="panel lighting-panel">
  <div class="panel-scroll">
  <div class="heading"><h1>Light &amp; atmosphere</h1><p>Changes save automatically.</p></div>
  <div class="light-row"><label>Ambient light</label><b id="ambient-value"/><input id="ambient" light="0" type="range" min="0.25" max="3" step="0.01"/><input id="ambient-number" light="0" type="text" maxlength="6"/></div>
  <div class="light-row"><label>Sun intensity</label><b id="sun-strength-value"/><input id="sun-strength" light="1" type="range" min="0" max="3" step="0.01"/><input id="sun-strength-number" light="1" type="text" maxlength="6"/></div>
  <div class="light-row" title="Atmospheric fog distance in blocks. Does not change the loaded world or lighting reach."><label for="fog-distance">Fog distance</label><b id="fog-distance-value"/><input id="fog-distance" light="2" type="range" min="64" max="2048" step="1"/><input id="fog-distance-number" light="2" type="text" maxlength="7"/></div>
  <h2>Atmosphere</h2>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="0" id="live-fog" class="setting toggle"><span>Distance fog</span><b id="live-fog-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="1" id="live-clouds" class="setting toggle"><span>Clouds</span><b id="live-clouds-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="2" id="live-sky" class="setting toggle"><span>Sky gradient</span><b id="live-sky-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="3" id="live-stars" class="setting toggle"><span>Stars</span><b id="live-stars-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="4" id="live-sun" class="setting toggle"><span>Sun</span><b id="live-sun-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-atmo" atmo="5" id="live-moon" class="setting toggle"><span>Moon</span><b id="live-moon-value"/></button>
  <h2>Shadows &amp; reflections</h2>
  <button action="cycle-shadow-quality" id="shadow-quality" class="setting" title="RT sun uses Low 1, Medium 2, High 4, Ultra 8 stable conservative rays at native shading size. High preserves the established path. Raster fallback uses Low 512 / 1 tap, Medium and High 1024 / 3x3 PCF, Ultra 2048 / 5x5 PCF. Ultra checks more occluders and can darken penumbrae; Low has hard shadow edges."><span>Shadow quality</span><b id="shadow-quality-value"/></button>
  <button action="cycle-reflection-quality" id="reflection-quality" class="setting" title="Map RT reflections: Low uses one-third width and height with 2 temporal directions, Medium half width and height with 2 directions, High half width and height with 4 directions, Ultra native shading size with 8 directions and 2 fresh rays per frame. Scene output remains native; lower tiers trade reflected detail and convergence for ray cost."><span>Map reflection quality</span><b id="reflection-quality-value"/></button>
  <p id="ray-quality-help" class="fsr-help">Shadow and reflection tiers are independent of voxel lighting. Reflection reconstruction does not reduce scene output resolution. Ultra spends more GPU time; no tier guarantees a frame rate. Water retains its separate single-ray reflection path.</p>
  <div class="light-row" title="Sun caster fade distance from the shaded surface, in blocks. 0 selects the raster fallback when enabled. Occlusion queries keep the full scene range; distant blocker visibility fades out near this limit."><label for="live-shadow-distance">Sun shadow distance</label><b id="live-shadow-distance-value"/><input id="live-shadow-distance" live="0" type="range" min="0" max="1024" step="1"/><input id="live-shadow-distance-number" live="0" type="text" maxlength="4"/></div>
  <div class="light-row" title="Maximum map-material and water reflection ray length, in blocks. 0 disables geometry reflections. Longer rays can reach more distant loaded geometry."><label for="live-reflection-distance">Reflection ray length</label><b id="live-reflection-distance-value"/><input id="live-reflection-distance" live="1" type="range" min="0" max="1024" step="1"/><input id="live-reflection-distance-number" live="1" type="text" maxlength="4"/></div>
  <p id="lighting-scene-status" class="fsr-help"/>
  <p class="fsr-help">Global illumination uses the loaded world geometry. Ray lengths do not load terrain. View distance determines available geometry; streaming can temporarily reduce it. Longer rays can increase tracing cost. Anti Aliasing render scale also affects per-pixel shadow and reflection cost.</p>
  <h2>Renderer</h2>
  <button action="toggle-ray-tracing-live" id="live-ray-tracing" class="setting toggle" title="Controls ray-traced sun and local shadows and reflections. World global illumination continues using hardware ray tracing. Saved ranges and quality choices are retained when switched off."><span>Ray-traced effects</span><b id="live-ray-tracing-value"/></button>
  <button action="toggle-raster-sun" id="live-raster-sun" class="setting toggle" title="Clipmap sun shadow fallback when traced shadows are off, unavailable, or waiting for complete geometry. This saved fallback preference can be changed while ray tracing is on."><span>Raster sun shadows</span><b id="live-raster-sun-value"/></button>
  <button action="cycle-lighting-debug" id="lighting-debug" class="setting" title="Cycles voxel lighting and ray-tracing diagnostics. Ray views need their corresponding lighting features enabled."><span>Debug view</span><b id="lighting-debug-value"/></button>
  <div class="footer"><button action="close-lighting" id="close-lighting" class="primary">Return to world</button><small>F6 or Escape to close</small></div>
  </div>
</div></div>
</body>
</rml>
